 ],
 "puzzleThemes": [],
 "intro": {
  "text": "In the Queen's Gambit Declined, Black answers White's 2.c4 (the c-pawn to c4) with 2...e6 (the e-pawn to e6). The e-pawn backs up the pawn on d5, so Black keeps a pawn in the centre and the bishop on f8 can come out. The cost is the other bishop: the pawn on e6 shuts in the bishop on c8. You develop the pieces on your kingside, the half of the board where your king starts (to develop a knight or bishop is to bring it off its starting square), then castle, and then look for a way to bring that bishop into play."
 },
